<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Antidraw collects when you use the app, sign in with Google and publish, and what we do with it."
  updated="November 4, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy covers Antidraw: the desktop app, this website at antidraw.com, the Antidraw account you create by signing in
    with Google, and the sites you publish to <code>antidraw.app</code>. Antidraw is run by an individual based in India
    (“we”, “us”). If you have a question or a request about your data, email
    <a href="mailto:hello@antidraw.com">hello@antidraw.com</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    In short: your workspaces stay on your computer, we don't sell your data, and we only collect what we need to run
    sign-in and publishing and to understand how much the app gets used.
  </p>

  <h2>The desktop app</h2>
  <p>
    Antidraw runs on your computer. Your workspaces, components, canvases and chat history are stored on your device. We
    don't receive them unless you publish a site (see below).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Your coding agent.</strong> Antidraw works with Claude Code, which runs on your computer with your own Anthropic
    account. Your prompts, and the code and files the agent reads, go from your computer to Anthropic under your agreement
    with Anthropic. They don't go through our servers, and we don't see them. Anthropic's handling of that data is covered by
    <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Anthropic's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Usage analytics.</strong> Each time you send a message to the agent, the app sends a usage event to PostHog, our
    product analytics provider. The event says that a message was sent, and includes the email address of the Claude account
    you're signed into, that account's organization, subscription type and API provider, plus the app version and your
    operating system. <strong>It never includes your messages, code or files.</strong> We use these events to understand how
    many people use Antidraw and how much they use it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Updates.</strong> The app checks GitHub for new releases and downloads updates from there, so GitHub sees your IP
    address and the app's version when it does. GitHub's handling of that is covered by
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Antidraw account</h2>
  <p>
    You only need an account to publish. When you sign in with Google, you allow us to see your basic profile and email address
    (the <code>openid</code>, <code>email</code> and <code>profile</code> permissions). We store:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, email address, whether Google has verified that email, and your profile picture's URL;</li>
    <li>your Google account ID, which links your Google account to your Antidraw account;</li>
    <li>the tokens Google issues when you sign in. We don't use them to access anything else in your Google account;</li>
    <li>
      for each signed-in session: when it started and when it expires, the IP address it signed in from, and your
      browser's or app's user agent.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this information to sign you in, keep you signed in, show you which account you're using, link your published sites
    to you, and protect the service against abuse. We don't ask Google for any other data, and we don't use your email for
    marketing.
  </p>

  <h3>Google user data</h3>
  <p>
    Antidraw's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including its Limited Use requirements. We use Google user data only to provide sign-in. We don't sell it, use it for
    advertising, or share it with anyone except the infrastructure providers listed below, which store it for us.
  </p>

  <h2>Sites you publish</h2>
  <p>When you publish a workspace, we store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the site's title and its address (its slug);</li>
    <li>the built files of your components and your canvas;</li>
    <li>the source code the site was built from, in a git repository, and a record of each publish.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Published sites are public.</strong> Anyone with the link can view them at <code>&lt;slug&gt;.antidraw.app</code>
    and on their share page at <code>antidraw.com/s/&lt;slug&gt;</code>. We keep the source each version was built from so the
    site can be rebuilt, and Antidraw may let other people view or remix a published site from that source. Don't publish
    anything you aren't happy to make public, including secrets such as API keys or passwords.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    antidraw.com uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page views and measures page performance without cookies and
    without identifying you. Cloudflare, which hosts the site, also processes your IP address to serve and protect it. The
    website doesn't set cookies. When you sign in, your browser stores a sign-in cookie for api.antidraw.com, which is used
    only to keep you signed in.
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <p>We don't sell your personal data. We share it only with these providers, and only so they can run Antidraw for us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosts the website, the API, our database and published sites, and provides website analytics.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong>: provides sign-in.</li>
    <li><strong>PostHog</strong> (US): stores the desktop app's usage events.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub</strong>: hosts app downloads and updates.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may store and process data outside your country, including in the United States. We may also disclose
    information if the law requires it, or to protect Antidraw, our users or the public from fraud or abuse.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account and session information: for as long as your account exists.</li>
    <li>Published sites, their files and their source: until you ask us to remove them or delete your account.</li>
    <li>Usage events: for as long as they are useful for understanding usage, and at most as long as PostHog keeps them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you delete your account, we delete your account and session records, your published sites, their files and their
    source within 30 days. Copies in backups may remain for a short time after that until they are overwritten.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to access, correct or delete your personal data, to send you a copy of it, or to stop processing it. To do
    so, email <a href="mailto:hello@antidraw.com">hello@antidraw.com</a> from the email address on your account. To delete your
    account and everything you have published, email us and ask. We'll respond within 30 days. Depending on where you live, for
    example under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 or the EU and UK GDPR, you may have further rights,
    including the right to complain to your data protection authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also revoke Antidraw's access in your
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Google account settings</a>. This stops
    future sign-ins but doesn't delete the data we already hold, so email us for that.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    All traffic to our servers is encrypted in transit. The desktop app keeps its own sign-in token and doesn't share it with
    the web pages it shows. Access to the production systems is limited to us. No system is perfectly secure, but we'll let you
    know if a breach affects your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Antidraw isn't intended for anyone under 18, and we don't knowingly collect data from them. If you believe a child has
    given us personal data, email us and we'll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we'll update the date at the top of this page. If a change matters, for example if we start
    collecting a new kind of data, we'll also say so on this website or in the app before it takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions, requests or complaints about your data, including as our grievance contact under India's data protection
    law, email <a href="mailto:hello@antidraw.com">hello@antidraw.com</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
